        "id": "shipped",
        "layout": "table",
        "title": "The fittings that ship"
      },
      {
        "after": "shipped",
        "body": "One smithing step per fitting: the fitting's template, the decorated armor, and the material.\nEvery piece on the armor that has a place of that kind is offered the material, so one gem\nfills the stone of each piece that has one, or of the one socket you pick at the advanced\nsmithing table. **The same template with the third slot empty takes the fitting out again.**\nRe-applying a piece at its own socket template keeps what is set in its fittings, so changing\na circlet's metal does not cost the gem.\n",
        "id": "applying",
        "title": "Applying one"
      },
      {
        "after": "applying",
        "body": "A fitting is data: a pack declares a new one in its own `fitting` folder, names the tag or\nlist of materials it accepts, and gets its template from a recipe. A piece names the fittings\nit has and ships one greyscale **mask** per masked fitting, saying where on the piece that\nmaterial goes. An effect can be gated on a fitting's value. The\n[authoring guide](/wiki/authoring/) covers the files; the [editor](/wiki/editor/) paints the\nmasks and previews any material in them live.\n",
        "id": "authors",
        "title": "For pack authors"
      }
    ],
